{"id":"travel-gifts-lobbyists-aboard","title":"Who travelled with officials on trips others paid for","question":"When an elected officer accepts travel paid by someone else, who goes along, and do the lobbyists on the trip contact that officer more afterwards?","finding":"34 Gifts of Travel filings list companions (375 rows). 17 list registered lobbyists or campaign consultants, or their staff; registered lobbyists filled 56 places, most on San Francisco Chamber of Commerce trips. In the lobbying contact log those lobbyists reported 15 contacts with the same officer in the year after the trip and 15 in the year before: no rise.","how":"Accompanying Persons (gqui-q3n5) joined to the Gifts of Travel filings (snqf-y894) by DocuSign ID. Categories are the filer's own: A City filer, B registered lobbyist or campaign consultant, C employee or owner of one, D employee of the payer. Each category-B companion's contacts with the officer (by surname) were counted in the lobbyist activity file, 365 days either side of the start date.","limits":"A filing is the disclosure Section 3.216(d) requires; travel paid by a non-profit host is permitted when filed. Contacts are matched on names; a lobbyist who registers under another spelling is missed. Some trips appear twice (an original and an amended filing, or two officers on one trip). Companions who are not lobbyists or officials are counted, not named.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"date","t":"Trip began","type":"date"},{"k":"officer","t":"Elected officer","type":"person"},{"k":"payer","t":"Paid by","type":"org"},{"k":"amount","t":"Amount","type":"usd"},{"k":"persons","t":"Companions listed","type":"int"},{"k":"cityFilers","t":"City filers","type":"int"},{"k":"lobbyists","t":"Registered lobbyists or consultants","type":"int"},{"k":"lobbyistStaff","t":"Their staff","type":"int"},{"k":"payerStaff","t":"Payer's staff","type":"int"},{"k":"before","t":"Lobbyist contacts, year before","type":"int"},{"k":"after","t":"Year after","t